<urn:atm:triage:finding/AX6-QA4-001>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AX6-QA4-001" ;
  triage:title "RULE-011: live_surface_json() in crates/atm/tests/cli_surface.rs spawns `atm __dump-cli-surface --format json` with no ATM_HOME/ATM_CONFIG_HOME/ATM_LOG_DIR/ATM_TEAMS_DIR isolation" ;
  triage:description "crates/atm/tests/cli_surface.rs:49 live_surface_json() spawns the atm binary (`__dump-cli-surface --format json`) with zero environment isolation. Every non-help/non-version subcommand runs init_observability() before dispatch (crates/atm/src/main.rs:216, run() at 190-233), and home::host_log_dir() (crates/atm-core/src/home.rs:170-192) falls back to the real user home .atm/logs when ATM_LOG_DIR is unset, so this spawn performs a durable write into the ambient ATM home; it is masked only by CI runners having an ephemeral HOME. Remediation: the same tempfile::tempdir() + Command::env() pattern already used in peer_cli.rs and compose_passthrough.rs (ATM_HOME, ATM_CONFIG_HOME, ATM_LOG_DIR, ATM_TEAMS_DIR). The sibling --version spawn at cli_surface.rs:67 was checked by arch-qa and needs no isolation (clap DisplayVersion short-circuits before init_observability); do not record it as an occurrence." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-ax" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "arch-qa" ;
  triage:severity "blocking" ;
  triage:repeatable true ;
  triage:sweepScope "crate" ;
  triage:status "fixed" ;
  triage:closedAt "2026-09-05T20:21:05Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:closedBy "quality-mgr" ;
  triage:closureNote "Closure confirmed by quality-mgr AX.6 QA-5 recheck (QA-AX6-R5-1788639500) at head 5120e0800; fixed by arch-ctm fix pass GO-AX6-FIX4-1788639030 (Completion c24). Report: PR #1204 comment 5554531804. Sprint verdict PASS 0/0/0." ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-09-05T20:15:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
